    "description": "Company Overview Kadisco Paint and Adhesive Industry S.C., formerly known as Kadisco Chemical Industry PLC, is a privately owned company located in the Akaki Kality Industrial Zone of Addis Ababa, Ethiopia. The company's history dates to the late 1960s, when it started as a small automotive parts dealership operating in one of the busiest commercial areas of Addis Ababa. In 1979, the company was officially registered as a manufacturer of adhesives and glue. Over the years, Kadisco expanded its operations and gradually developed into one of Ethiopia's leading paint manufacturers, diversifying its product portfolio and strengthening its market presence. In February 2015, Asian Paints Ltd. acquired a 51% stake in Kadisco Paint and Adhesive Industry S.C., and the company subsequently became known as Kadisco Asian Paints. Asian Paints is India's leading paint company and the second-largest paint company in Asia. The company has built a strong reputation for professionalism, innovation, rapid growth, and creating long-term shareholder value. Asian Paints operates in several countries across Asia, the Middle East, and Africa, with 26 paint manufacturing facilities worldwide and a presence in more than 65 countries, serving millions of customers across the globe. Today, Kadisco Asian Paints produces a comprehensive range of paints and coatings for the decorative, construction, industrial, and automotive sectors. The company also manufactures wood and concrete lacquers, as well as adhesives serving the wood, furniture, and leather industries, contributing significantly to Ethiopia's manufacturing sector and economic development. Job Description: Executive I – Store Job Identification Job Title: Executive I – Store Department: Stores Location: Addis Ababa Number of Positions: 1 Reports To: Senior Executive – Stores Job Purpose To support the Senior Executive – Stores in the day-to-day store and inventory management activities, including receiving, storing, issuing, and handling materials, SAP transactions, inventory control, documentation, stock reconciliation, and dispatch support while ensuring inventory accuracy and compliance with company procedures. Major Roles and Responsibilities Support the daily operations of the Store under the supervision of the Senior Executive – Stores. Participate in the receipt, storage, issuance, and movement of raw materials, packaging materials, and other Store items. Check received materials against relevant delivery documents and Store records. Ensure proper identification, labeling, arrangement, stacking, and storage of materials. Issue materials to Production and other departments based on properly authorized requests. Support material handling and internal movement of materials between Store and Production areas. Record receipts, issues, transfers, returns, and other inventory transactions in SAP. Conduct regular physical inventory counts and support stock reconciliation against SAP/system balances. Identify and report damaged, excess, obsolete, slow-moving, non-moving, or short materials. Maintain proper Store documentation, including GRNs, issue notes, transfer documents, return notes, and inventory records. Ensure proper filing and traceability of Store documents for operational and audit requirements. Support dispatch activities whenever required, including checking, preparation, documentation, and loading support. Coordinate with Production, Procurement, Supply Chain, Finance, Quality, Security, and other departments concerned. Maintain good housekeeping, material organization, and safety standards within the Store. Prepare and submit daily, weekly, and monthly Store and inventory reports. Immediately report any inventory discrepancy, material damage, shortage, or other Store-related issue to the Senior Executive – Stores. Perform other Store and inventory-related activities assigned by the Senior Executive – Stores.",
