    "description": "Logistics, Procurement & Fleet Management Officer Organic Liquid Fertilizer Producing PLC (Eco Green) Duty Station Addis Ababa – Head Office Reports To Logistics & Procurement Department Manager Employment Type Full-time Position Purpose The Logistics, Procurement & Fleet Management Officer is responsible for executing transparent, cost-effective procurement; coordinating deliveries and transport dispatch; maintaining the company’s fleet in safe, serviceable, and legally compliant condition; and controlling trip-level costs and fleet performance. The officer ensures that purchases, transport movements, vehicle maintenance, fuel use, goods receipt, and fleet-related expenses are properly planned, documented, approved, and recorded in the company’s ERP system. ERP proficiency and the ability to work in a fully digital, system-based environment are mandatory. The position is operational and hands-on, with a strong emphasis on cost control, timely execution, documentation, integrity, and measurable results. Key Responsibilities 1. Procurement, Supplier Sourcing & Purchasing Control Execute approved procurement requirements across the company, including fermentation inputs, packaging materials (1L, 5L, and 25L containers, caps, labels, cartons), machinery and factory spare parts, laboratory supplies, vehicle parts and tires, and office consumables. Identify, assess, prequalify, and maintain an organized supplier database covering Addis Ababa and relevant regional markets; periodically evaluate supplier reliability, quality, price, lead time, and service. Obtain quotations and proforma invoices, prepare comparative bid analyses, negotiate prices, discounts, payment terms, delivery conditions, and warranties, and submit purchases for approval in accordance with company procedures. Prepare and follow up purchase requisitions, purchase orders, delivery schedules, and procurement records; ensure purchases are made only with proper authorization. Verify the completeness and validity of VAT and withholding-tax documentation and other required commercial documents before forwarding payment requests to Finance. Coordinate urgent purchases responsibly to minimize production interruptions, while ensuring approvals and documentation are not bypassed. Track procurement status from requisition through order, delivery, inspection, and handover; proactively report delays, price changes, and supply risks. 2. Transport, Dispatch & Delivery Operations Prepare and coordinate daily vehicle allocation, dispatch plans, routes, schedules, and driver assignments for raw-material movements to Tulefa and finished-product deliveries to distributors, regional hubs, commercial farms, and customers. Coordinate with the factory, warehouse/store, sales team, and drivers to ensure vehicles, products, loading plans, delivery documents, and destinations are ready before dispatch. Monitor departure and arrival times, route adherence, delivery completion, and customer handover; collect signed delivery notes, waybills, and other supporting documents. Prevent unauthorized vehicle use, unapproved route changes, undocumented trips, and incomplete delivery records. Arrange third-party transport when required; obtain and compare quotations, negotiate rates, confirm service terms, and evaluate outsourced transport against internal fleet costs and service reliability. Resolve delivery disruptions promptly and report significant delays, damages, shortages, or customer delivery issues. 3. Fleet Administration, Maintenance & Legal Compliance Maintain an accurate master register for every company vehicle, including vehicle identification, ownership documents, assigned driver, mileage, condition, service history, insurance, permits, and compliance status. Develop and maintain preventive-maintenance schedules based on mileage, time, manufacturer guidance, and vehicle condition; proactively schedule oil changes, servicing, tires, brakes, and repairs. Coordinate repairs and servicing with approved garages; obtain quotations where required, verify work performed and parts replaced, and check repair invoices before submission for payment. Ensure timely renewal and compliance of annual Bolo inspections, insurance, road-fund stickers, applicable transport permits, and driver licenses; maintain a compliance calendar and alert management before deadlines. Keep complete individual vehicle files and maintenance records, including inspection reports, garage quotations, invoices, approvals, and repair/servicing evidence. Monitor vehicle condition, safety, cleanliness, and readiness; immediately escalate serious defects, accidents, safety risks, or overdue compliance matters. 4. Trip Costing, Fuel Control & Fleet Performance Prepare a cost record for every trip, including fuel consumption and cost, driver allowances/per diem, loading and unloading expenses, tolls and other trip charges, and applicable maintenance/depreciation allocation where the company’s costing method requires it. Calculate and monitor key fleet indicators such as cost per kilometer, cost per liter or ton delivered, fuel consumption, vehicle utilization, payload/load factor, trip turnaround time, and cost of internal transport versus outsourced freight. Compare actual trip costs with planned costs, commercial transport quotations, and delivery economics; identify and report loss-making, inefficient, or unusually expensive trips. Reconcile fuel receipts, issued fuel, odometer readings, trip logs, and GPS records where available; investigate unexplained variances, excessive consumption, idle time, unauthorized trips, or suspected misuse. Optimize vehicle utilization, loading efficiency, dispatch scheduling, and return-load/backhaul opportunities to reduce empty trips and unnecessary transport costs. Submit accurate weekly operational updates and a monthly fleet performance and cost report, including key variances, maintenance status, compliance renewals, cost trends, and improvement recommendations. 5. Goods Receipt, Inventory Handover & Documentation Physically verify purchased goods against purchase orders, supplier delivery documents, quantities, specifications, and visible condition before accepting or handing them over. Coordinate with the Tulefa Store and Addis Ababa office to complete Goods Received Notes (GRNs), Goods Issue Vouchers (GIVs), delivery notes, and relevant stock or handover records. Report shortages, damage, incorrect items, quality concerns, or discrepancies immediately; ensure such issues are documented and resolved before acceptance or payment processing. Ensure all procurement, dispatch, trip, fuel, maintenance, and goods-handover records are complete, accurate, properly filed, and entered into the ERP system promptly. 6. ERP-Based Execution, Reporting & Accountability Record and update procurement requests, supplier quotations, comparative analyses, purchase orders, deliveries, vehicle assignments, trips, fuel records, maintenance schedules, compliance renewals, expenses, and handovers in the ERP or designated company systems. Use ERP records as the official operational record; avoid undocumented purchases, trips, expenses, maintenance work, or handovers. Maintain organized digital and physical records that can be verified, audited, and retrieved without delay. Follow approved procedures, delegated authority, internal controls, deadlines, and reporting lines; escalate risks and exceptions promptly. Carry out other related duties assigned by the Logistics & Procurement Department Manager that are consistent with the position.",
